course: dictionary
lesson: 9039
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. «In Athens women, slaves and foreigners could not vote.» Here a slave is a person who is owned by another person and forced to work without pay or freedom. The words around it, vote and rule by the people, give you the clue.
explain: The same word can be used in a different way. «Dad slaved over the dinner» uses slaved as an informal verb. It means Dad worked very hard for a long time. Nobody owned Dad, so the meaning is not about owning people. Read the whole sentence before you choose a meaning.
explain: A phrase can change the meaning too. A slave to something means you are controlled by it, like a slave to fashion. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it makes the sentence silly, try the next meaning.
fact: A slave is a person who is owned by another person and forced to work without pay or freedom.
fact: «Slave» can also be an informal verb: «slave away» means to work very hard.
fact: A slave driver is a boss who makes people work too hard.
fact: Slavery is against the law today, but forced labour still exists, and people campaign to stop it.
fact: The slave trade took millions of young people from West and Central Africa by force, and brave people worked to end it.
exercise: «In Athens women, slaves and foreigners could not vote.» What is a slave in this sentence? | A very old castle | *A person owned by another and forced to work without pay or freedom | A person who works very hard for fun | A person who votes in every election
exercise: «Dad slaved over the dinner.» What does slaved mean here? | Sat down and rested | Was controlled by fashion | *Worked very hard for a long time | Was owned by someone else
exercise: «She is a slave to fashion.» What does this suggest? | *Fashion controls her choices | She designs clothes for a living | She is very rich | She always wears the same coat
test: Which phrase means a boss who makes people work too hard? | A slave to fashion | *A slave driver | A slave trade | Free the slaves
test: In which sentence does slave mean to work very hard? | *I will slave away on my homework tonight | Ordinary people signed petitions to end slavery | The slave trade caused wars and raids | They called it democracy, rule by the people
exam: Using the context, what does slave mean in «Paul taught that all are one in Christ, neither Jew nor Greek, slave nor free»? | A person who works very hard | A person controlled by fashion | *A person owned by another and forced to work without pay or freedom | A boss who makes people work too hard
